"""Localized copy generated by `BankruptcyAnalysisService`.

Everything this service produces as prose — missing items, warnings,
discussion points, chapter questions, next steps — reaches a human unchanged.
It travels through `CaseAnalysisDto` into `CaseContextDto`, and from there the
deterministic draft turns `next_steps` into the assistant's suggested-action
labels and `warnings` into `AssistantResponse.warnings`.

Until 4.2.0 all of it was hardcoded Spanish, so an English session received
Spanish action labels — one half of the language leak the live agent run
recorded (`changes/chat-modal-centered.md`, defect 3). The other half is a
model emitting labels in the wrong language, which is handled in the agent
prompts.

Kept as one flat catalogue rather than scattered across the service so that a
missing translation is visible by reading two columns, and so `ruff` and the
type checker see every key.

**`required_evidence` is deliberately absent.** Those strings are matched
word-by-word against `EVIDENCE_TYPE_LABELS` by
`BankruptcyAnalysisService._evidence_matches` to compute `evidence_score`;
translating one side without the other would silently zero that score. That is
a separate defect from this one and is left recorded rather than half-fixed.
"""

